<title>PHILIPPINES: Sinophil gets SEC nod for conversion.</title>
<headline>Sinophil gets SEC nod for conversion.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sinophil Corp said on Tuesday the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) had approved its conversion into a holding firm from an oil exploration company.</p>
<p>The company said it had also obtained SEC approval for an increase in its authorised capital stock to 20 billion pesos from two billion. The shares will be divided into 14 billion common and six billion preferred.</p>
<p>Sinophil also secured approval for the change in the par value of its shares to one peso from 0.01 peso per share.</p>
<p>Sinophil is a unit of Belle Corp.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (63 2) 841 8939 Fax 817 6267</p>
